OOGFOSWorldScriptsInit creates a read-only nonconfigurable global
worldScripts; OOGFOSWorldScriptsRegister binds real per-script JS objects
under original world-script names. It supports hyphens and dots in names,
rejects illegal/injection-like syntax and refuses duplicate names rather
than silently replacing read-only entries. Entries are enumerable,
read-only and nonconfigurable. Native guest verified two independent
scripts, property descriptors, host ship bounty=42 and names:
'oolite-world-a', 'oolite.oxp-b'. Duplicate returned JSERR_TYPE=5;
unsafe name returned JSERR_BADARGS=4. Script and global object lifetimes
are owned by the single canonical JSTask.

This is the explicit C source-level GFOS equivalent of the original
OOJSWorldScripts registry. The full original PlayerEntity/Universe scripts
are not yet ported or runnable.
